# OM Screener — Cursor Rules
# These are injected into every Cursor session for this project.
# Zoé and Cursor share this context.

## What we're building
An AI agent that takes a CRE Offering Memorandum (PDF) as input, extracts
key financial and property metrics, scores the deal against Will's buy criteria,
and outputs a structured one-page verdict. Built in n8n + Python. Filmed for LinkedIn.

## Architecture (5 discrete stages — build and test each before wiring)
1. PDF ingestion → raw text extraction
2. LLM structured extraction → typed JSON output (metrics)
3. Scoring layer → verdict against buy criteria
4. Output formatter → human-readable summary
5. Delivery → Telegram notification

## Data model (input/output schemas live in data-model.md — read it before coding)

## Stack
- n8n for orchestration (self-hosted, localhost:5678)
- Python for PDF extraction (PyPDF2 or pdfplumber)
- Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 for LLM stages
- Prompts live in /prompts/*.md — never hardcode prompts in code
- Tests live in /tests/ — each stage has its own test before wiring

## Coding standards
- One n8n node = one responsibility
- All LLM prompts are files, not inline strings
- Every stage tested on 3 real OMs before connecting to the next
- Human review gate after stage 2 (LLM extraction) before scoring fires
- No credentials in code — use n8n credential store

## CRE domain context
- Will has 25 years of CRE experience + completed Fast Track underwriting course
- Buy criteria will be specified in buy-criteria.md (Will fills this in)
- Key metrics to extract: NOI, cap rate, occupancy %, debt terms (LTV, DSCR, rate),
  vintage, market/submarket, property type, asking price, price/unit or price/SF
- Red flags: vacancy >15%, deferred maintenance signals, thin DSCR (<1.20), tertiary market

## Code Review Gate (MANDATORY)
Before this stage advances to "Tested":
- All src/ files and prompts/ files must pass a Codex 5.3 review
- Trigger: tell Zoé "Z, run Codex review on stage-1"
- Reviewer model: openai/gpt-5.3-codex (adversarial second LLM)
- Reports saved to: code-review/reports/
- FAIL verdict = fix BLOCKERs and re-run before any real OM testing
- See code-review/GATE.md for full process

## Tone
This is Will's project. Code should be readable and explainable — it'll be filmed.
